      "text": "H.J.Res. 106, sponsored by @SenDanSullivan, Sen. @lisamurkowski, and @RepNickBegich, overturns the Biden-era Central Yukon Resource Management Plan, which shut down more than 13 million acres in one of Alaska’s most impoverished regions.\n\n— Restores access to vital lands for energy, minerals, and infrastructure.\n— Supports major projects like the Ambler Access and Alaska LNG, which will create jobs and strengthen Alaska’s economy.\n— Puts Alaska back on the path toward economic independence —powered by responsible development and local decision-making.\n— Strengthens national security, lowers costs for working families, and ensures Alaskans shape their future.\n\nH.J.Res. 131, sponsored by the same, reverses the Biden Administration’s regulations on the 1002 Area of Alaska’s North Slope — which, because of its tremendous strategic value and estimated 7.7 billion barrels of oil, Congress explicitly set aside more than 40 years ago for exploration and potential development.",
      "text_resolved": "H.J.Res. 106, sponsored by @SenDanSullivan, Sen. @lisamurkowski, and @RepNickBegich, overturns the Biden-era Central Yukon Resource Management Plan, which shut down more than 13 million acres in one of Alaska’s most impoverished regions.\n\n— Restores access to vital lands for energy, minerals, and infrastructure.\n— Supports major projects like the Ambler Access and Alaska LNG, which will create jobs and strengthen Alaska’s economy.\n— Puts Alaska back on the path toward economic independence —powered by responsible development and local decision-making.\n— Strengthens national security, lowers costs for working families, and ensures Alaskans shape their future.\n\nH.J.Res. 131, sponsored by the same, reverses the Biden Administration’s regulations on the 1002 Area of Alaska’s North Slope — which, because of its tremendous strategic value and estimated 7.7 billion barrels of oil, Congress explicitly set aside more than 40 years ago for exploration and potential development.",
