      "text": "H.J.Res. 130, sponsored by @SenJohnBarrasso, @SenLummis, and @RepHageman, overturns restrictions that prohibited future coal leasing applications through 2038 in Wyoming’s Powder River Basin — a state that produces 40% of the nation’s coal.\n\n— Keeps energy prices affordable and reliable by ensuring access to 48.12 billion short tons of coal, enough supply to meet U.S. coal demand for the next 116 years.\n— Protects 4,122 jobs in rural Wyoming, $1.9 billion in labor output through 2048, and millions of dollars in state revenue used to fund public K-12 education.\n\nWyoming has been the leading coal producing state since 1986; in 2024, Wyoming produced 191 million tons of coal and shipped 171 million tons to 26 states",
